@userToken = eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJ1c2VySWQiOiI4NjVjNTRhYS1mMDJiLTRlYTgtYTdiOS0wN2QzMWU2NWY3OTIiLCJyb2xlIjoidXNlciIsImlhdCI6MTc5MjY1NjI2MSwiZXhwIjoxNzk1MjQ4MjYxfQ.8T0UAPopZfLWNsUpvL-lWlD8s71F5dtf43F8TUfocXA

### =================================================================
### 1. REQ: Logging, Health & Correlation (X-Request-Id)
### =================================================================

### 1.1 Health check - verify 200 OK and X-Request-Id header in response
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### =================================================================
### 2. REQ: Authentication & Authorization Failures (401, 403)
### =================================================================

### 2.1 Missing authorization token - expect 401 Unauthorized
GET {{baseUrl}}/users

### 2.2 Invalid authorization token - expect 401 Unauthorized
GET {{baseUrl}}/users
Authorization: Bearer invalid.token.value

### 2.3 Login with incorrect password - expect 401 Unauthorized
POST {{baseUrl}}/users/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "id": "{{adminId}}",
    "password": "wrong-password"
}

### 2.4 User attempting admin action (Role check) - expect 403 Forbidden
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/users/{{userId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Unauthorized Update"
}

### =================================================================
### 3. REQ: Header & Parameter Validation (400, 415)
### =================================================================

### 3.1 Unsupported Media Type (non-JSON Content-Type) - expect 415
POST {{baseUrl}}/users/login
Content-Type: text/plain

invalid-body

### 3.2 Invalid UUID parameter format - expect 400 Bad Request
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/123-not-a-valid-uuid
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 3.3 Missing required field 'id' on login - expect 400 Bad Request
POST {{baseUrl}}/users/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "password": "1234"
}

### 3.4 Missing required field 'password' on login - expect 400 Bad Request
POST {{baseUrl}}/users/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "id": "{{adminId}}"
}

### 3.5 PATCH with empty body - expect 400 Bad Request
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/users/{{adminId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 3.6 PATCH with disallowed field (attempting to alter role) - expect 400 Bad Request
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/users/{{adminId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "role": "super-admin"
}

### 3.7 PATCH with invalid field data (blank name) - expect 400 Bad Request
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/users/{{adminId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "   "
}

### =================================================================
### 4. REQ: Malformed Requests (400 Bad Request)
### =================================================================

### 4.1 Malformed JSON body - expect 400 Bad Request
POST {{baseUrl}}/users/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "id":
}

### =================================================================
### 5. REQ: Missing Resources (404 Not Found)
### =================================================================

### 5.1 Nonexistent user UUID - expect 404 Not Found
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/{{nonexistentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 5.2 Unknown route URL - expect 404 Not Found
GET {{baseUrl}}/unknown-route

### =================================================================
### 6. REQ: Unsupported HTTP Methods (405 Method Not Allowed)
### =================================================================

### 6.1 Unsupported method on /users collection (PUT) - expect 405 (Allow: GET)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/users
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 6.2 Unsupported method on auth route /users/login (GET) - expect 405 (Allow: POST)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/login

### 6.3 Unsupported method on health route (POST) - expect 405 (Allow: GET)
POST {{baseUrl}}/health

### =================================================================
### 7. REQ: Sensitive Information Protection (No Password Leak)
### =================================================================

### 7.1 Verify user response strips password hash - expect 200 with safe fields only
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/{{adminId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
